        "text": "$\\frac13$"
      },
      {
        "key": "B",
        "text": "$\\frac12$"
      },
      {
        "key": "C",
        "text": "3"
      },
      {
        "key": "D",
        "text": "2"
      },
      {
        "key": "E",
        "text": "1"
      }
    ],
    "answer": "E",
    "acceptedAnswers": null,
    "answerUnit": null,
    "solutions": [
      {
        "title": "Multiply the fractions",
        "body": "Half of a third of a quarter is $\\frac12\\cdot\\frac13\\cdot\\frac14 = \\frac1{24}$ of a day. A day has 24 hours, so this is 1 hour.\n\n**Answer: (E) 1**"
      },
      {
        "title": "Work backwards from 24 hours",
        "body": "A quarter of 24 hours is 6 hours, a third of that is 2 hours, and half of that is 1 hour.\n\n**Answer: (E) 1**"
      }
    ],
