    "type": "mc",
    "prompt": "The diagram shows a cube with sides of length 12 cm. An ant is walking across the cube's surface from A to G using the path shown in bold. How far will it have to walk?",
    "image": "qimages/kangaroo/ca-2011-training-g0708/q02.webp",
    "choices": [
      {
        "key": "A",
        "text": "48 cm"
      },
      {
        "key": "B",
        "text": "40 cm"
      },
      {
        "key": "C",
        "text": "50 cm"
      },
      {
        "key": "D",
        "text": "60 cm"
      },
      {
        "key": "E",
        "text": "It is impossible to determine"
      }
    ],
    "answer": "D",
    "acceptedAnswers": null,
    "answerUnit": null,
    "solutions": [
      {
        "title": "Add the pieces",
        "body": "The path is $AB + BC + CD + DE + EF + FG$. The segments $AB$, $CD$, $EF$ and $FG$ are each a full edge (or parallel to an edge across a face), so each is 12 cm. $BC$ and $DE$ are parallel pieces on the front face that together span its width: $BC + DE = 12$ cm. Total: $4\\cdot12 + 12 = 60$ cm.\n\n**Answer: (D) 60 cm**"
      }
    ],
    "topics": [
