        "title": "Use the angle sum",
        "body": "Let $\\angle B = x$. Then $\\angle A = 3x$ and $\\angle C = 2\\cdot3x = 6x$. The angles of a triangle add up to $180^\\circ$: $x + 3x + 6x = 10x = 180^\\circ$, so $x = 18^\\circ$ and $\\angle A = 54^\\circ$.\n\n**Answer: (C) $54^\\circ$**"
      }
