    "type": "mc",
    "prompt": "Which of the following numbers is odd for every integer $n$?",
    "image": null,
    "choices": [
      {
        "key": "A",
        "text": "$2011n$"
      },
      {
        "key": "B",
        "text": "$n^2 + 2011$"
      },
      {
        "key": "C",
        "text": "$n^3$"
      },
      {
        "key": "D",
        "text": "$n + 2012$"
      },
      {
        "key": "E",
        "text": "$2n^2 + 2011$"
      }
    ],
    "answer": "E",
    "acceptedAnswers": null,
    "answerUnit": null,
    "solutions": [
      {
        "title": "Parity",
        "body": "$2n^2$ is always even, and even + odd is odd, so $2n^2 + 2011$ is odd for every $n$.\n\nThe others fail: for even $n$, $2011n$, $n^3$ and $n + 2012$ are even; for odd $n$, $n^2 + 2011$ is odd + odd = even.\n\n**Answer: (E) $2n^2 + 2011$**"
      },
      {
        "title": "Test n = 0 and n = 1",
        "body": "With $n = 0$: $0, 2011, 0, 2012, 2011$ — A, C and D are even. With $n = 1$: B gives $2012$, even. Only E remains, and it is always odd because $2n^2$ is even.\n\n**Answer: (E) $2n^2 + 2011$**"
      }
    ],
    "topics": [
      "number-theory"
    ],
    "difficulty": 2,
