        "text": "$600^\\circ$"
      },
      {
        "key": "E",
        "text": "$720^\\circ$"
      }
    ],
    "answer": "E",
    "acceptedAnswers": null,
    "answerUnit": null,
    "solutions": [
      {
        "title": "Angles at A",
        "body": "The five triangles have total angle sum $5\\cdot180^\\circ = 900^\\circ$. Their angles at $A$ are not marked. The lines through $A$ make vertical (opposite) angles: each angle at $A$ inside a triangle is opposite an equal angle at $A$ that lies outside the triangles, and these 10 angles fill the full $360^\\circ$ around $A$. So the triangles' angles at $A$ add up to $180^\\circ$.\n\nThe 10 marked angles add up to $900^\\circ - 180^\\circ = 720^\\circ$.\n\n**Answer: (E) $720^\\circ$**"
      }
    ],
