    "type": "mc",
    "prompt": "Charles tells the truth every other day; otherwise he lies. Today he stated exactly four of the following statements. Which one could he not have stated today?",
    "image": null,
    "choices": [
      {
        "key": "A",
        "text": "I have a prime number of friends."
      },
      {
        "key": "B",
        "text": "I have as many male friends as female."
      },
      {
        "key": "C",
        "text": "288 is divisible by 12."
      },
      {
        "key": "D",
        "text": "I always tell the truth."
      },
      {
        "key": "E",
        "text": "Three of my friends are older than me."
      }
    ],
    "answer": "C",
    "acceptedAnswers": null,
    "answerUnit": null,
    "solutions": [
      {
        "title": "Is today a truthful day?",
        "body": "Today Charles either tells the truth (all four statements true) or lies (all four false).\n\n- C is true ($288 = 12\\cdot24$) and D is false (he lies on some days).\n- Suppose he tells the truth today. Then D was not said, so he said A, B, C and E, all true. By B the number of his friends is even, and by A it is prime, so he has exactly 2 friends — but then E (three friends older than him) is impossible. Contradiction.\n- So he lies today, all four statements are false, and the true statement C is the one he did not say. (A, B, D, E can all be false at once, so this works.)\n\n**Answer: (C)**"
      }
    ],
    "topics": [
      "logic"
    ],
    "difficulty": 3,
    "duplicateOf": null,
    "reviewNote": null
  },
